============================================================
THREE GOLDEN RULES
============================================================

GOLDEN RULE #1 — DO NOT REDESIGN THE APP
------------------------------------------------------------
The desktop/laptop application already looks good.
Preserve ALL of the following:
- Existing colors, theme, typography, cards, shadows, gradients
- Existing icons, animations, navigation structure
- Existing branding, visual hierarchy, features, business logic

The objective is: SAME APPLICATION + ADAPTIVE LAYOUT.
NOT: NEW APPLICATION DESIGN.

GOLDEN RULE #2 — NEVER FIX MOBILE BY BREAKING DESKTOP
------------------------------------------------------------
Every responsive modification must be checked against desktop behavior.
A mobile fix must NOT destroy: Windows layout, desktop navigation, wide
dashboards, tables, existing desktop spacing, cards, or dialogs.
Use responsive branching:

    if (isCompact) → mobile layout
    else if (isMedium) → tablet layout
    else → existing desktop layout (UNTOUCHED)

GOLDEN RULE #3 — NO DEVICE-SPECIFIC HARD-CODED FIXES
------------------------------------------------------------
NEVER use:  if (width == 360)  or  if (device == "Samsung")
Build responsive rules based on AVAILABLE SPACE and CONTENT.
Prefer: LayoutBuilder, MediaQuery, Flexible, Expanded, Wrap,
ConstrainedBox, FractionallySizedBox, SafeArea, SingleChildScrollView.

