============================================================
SPECIFIC COMPONENT AUDIT RULES
============================================================

ROWS
------------------------------------------------------------
Every Row is a potential overflow source.
For every Row ask: Can these children fit on 320px?
Solutions: Flexible, Expanded, Wrap, responsive Column switch, horizontal scroll.
Desktop Row with side-by-side cards → Mobile stacked Column.
Do NOT globally replace Row→Column. Use responsive branching.

COLUMNS
------------------------------------------------------------
Check Columns for vertical overflow, especially:
Column + keyboard + forms + buttons.
Solution: Wrap in SingleChildScrollView where appropriate.

GRIDS
------------------------------------------------------------
Never use crossAxisCount: 4 everywhere.
Calculate crossAxisCount from available width:
    crossAxisCount = max(1, (availableWidth / minCardWidth).floor())
Or use SliverGrid with maxCrossAxisExtent.

TABLES
------------------------------------------------------------
VERY IMPORTANT for academy management.
Desktop: show all columns.
Mobile: EITHER horizontal scroll wrapper OR transform rows into cards.
Never compress 8 columns into 360px.
Preserve full desktop tables on desktop.

FORMS
------------------------------------------------------------
Desktop: multi-column (Name | Father Name, Phone | Class)
Mobile: single-column (Name, Father Name, Phone, Class)
Form fields must use full available width.
Forms MUST be scrollable (keyboard interaction).

DIALOGS
------------------------------------------------------------
Desktop desired width should be constrained:
    maxWidth = min(desktopDesiredWidth, availableWidth - 32)
Long dialog content must scroll.
Buttons should Wrap when insufficient horizontal space.

BOTTOM SHEETS
------------------------------------------------------------
Must respect SafeArea, keyboard, scrollability, viewport limits.

NAVIGATION
------------------------------------------------------------
Desktop: NavigationRail / Sidebar
Mobile: BottomNavigationBar / Drawer
Do NOT force desktop sidebar onto mobile.
Preserve desktop navigation on desktop.

APPBAR
------------------------------------------------------------
Long titles → Flexible + TextOverflow.ellipsis
Too many actions → overflow menu on compact
Preserve full AppBar on desktop.

BUTTONS
------------------------------------------------------------
Multiple buttons in a Row may overflow on mobile.
Solution: Wrap widget or stacked Column on compact.
Maintain minimum touch targets (44x44).

DROPDOWNS
------------------------------------------------------------
Long values must not overflow.
Use isExpanded: true where appropriate.

IMAGES
------------------------------------------------------------
Use BoxFit.cover / BoxFit.contain.
Images must not distort or overflow.
Use AspectRatio or ClipRRect where appropriate.

QR CODES
------------------------------------------------------------
Must remain: perfectly square, scannable, not clipped.
Responsive sizing: min(availableWidth * 0.7, 300)

SPACING
------------------------------------------------------------
Adaptive spacing:
    compact  → 12–16px padding
    medium   → 20–24px padding
    expanded → existing desktop spacing (unchanged)

TYPOGRAPHY
------------------------------------------------------------
Avoid extreme desktop-sized fonts on tiny screens.
Preserve hierarchy: Heading > Subheading > Body > Caption.
Do NOT make text unreadably small.
Do NOT globally disable accessibility text scaling.

